WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.121
Sightseeing and Tourist Places.

2
00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:06.689
Day 32 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.439 --> 00:00:09.463
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:17.529
Today's goal: buy tickets, hire a guide, ask about history and timings, take photos politely, and chat with other travellers.

5
00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:19.733
Part 1.

6
00:00:20.013 --> 00:00:20.973
Key words.

7
00:00:22.223 --> 00:00:23.588
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:44.839
Word or phrase, and Meaning. entry ticket or admission: ticket to go in. guided tour or audio guide: tour with a guide or recorded guide. opening hours or timings: when it's open. heritage site or monument or fort or temple: historic places. souvenir: a gift to remember the place. viewpoint: place

9
00:00:45.119 --> 00:00:51.839
with a good view. sunrise or sunset point: best place to watch the sun. itinerary: your travel plan.

10
00:00:53.189 --> 00:00:54.063
Part 2.

11
00:00:54.343 --> 00:00:55.559
Questions you'll ask.

12
00:00:56.809 --> 00:00:59.647
What are the timings? / What time does it close?

13
00:00:59.927 --> 00:01:01.591
How much is the entry ticket?

14
00:01:01.871 --> 00:01:03.855
Is there a separate ticket for cameras?

15
00:01:04.135 --> 00:01:05.479
Is there a guided tour?

16
00:01:05.759 --> 00:01:07.060
How long does it take?

17
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.236
In English?

18
00:01:08.516 --> 00:01:09.903
How old is this fort?

19
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:11.143
Who built it?

20
00:01:11.423 --> 00:01:13.001
What's the best time to visit?

21
00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:15.095
Could you take a photo of us, please?

22
00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.996
Can I take photos inside?

23
00:01:18.346 --> 00:01:19.775
What else should we see nearby?

24
00:01:20.055 --> 00:01:22.189
How do we get to the sunset point from here?

25
00:01:23.539 --> 00:01:24.435
Part 3.

26
00:01:24.715 --> 00:01:27.552
Conversation 1: hiring a guide at a fort.

27
00:01:28.802 --> 00:01:30.829
Here is how the conversation goes.

28
00:01:31.109 --> 00:01:32.858
Hello sir, do you want a guide?

29
00:01:33.138 --> 00:01:34.845
I speak English and Hindi.

30
00:01:35.125 --> 00:01:35.935
Maybe.

31
00:01:36.215 --> 00:01:39.351
How long is the tour, and how much do you charge?

32
00:01:39.631 --> 00:01:40.975
One and a half hours.

33
00:01:41.255 --> 00:01:43.154
800 rupeesfor your group.

34
00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.333
Is that for all four of us?

35
00:01:45.613 --> 00:01:47.106
Yes, for the whole group.

36
00:01:48.456 --> 00:01:50.056
The conversation continues.

37
00:01:50.336 --> 00:01:51.275
Okay.

38
00:01:51.555 --> 00:01:54.413
Could you also show us the best spots for photos?

39
00:01:54.693 --> 00:01:55.611
Of course.

40
00:01:55.891 --> 00:01:58.152
This fort was built in the 16th century.

41
00:01:58.432 --> 00:02:00.331
The palace inside is beautiful.

42
00:02:00.611 --> 00:02:01.613
Interesting!

43
00:02:01.893 --> 00:02:02.981
Who built it?

44
00:02:03.261 --> 00:02:04.563
Raja Man Singh.

45
00:02:04.843 --> 00:02:06.805
Come, let's start from the main gate.

46
00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:08.408
Great, let's go.

47
00:02:09.758 --> 00:02:10.675
Part 4.

48
00:02:10.955 --> 00:02:14.070
Conversation 2: asking a stranger for a photo.

49
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.347
Here is how the conversation goes.

50
00:02:17.627 --> 00:02:19.952
Excuse me, sorry to bother you.

51
00:02:20.232 --> 00:02:22.323
Could you take a photo of us, please?

52
00:02:22.603 --> 00:02:23.264
Sure!

53
00:02:23.544 --> 00:02:25.165
Portrait or landscape?

54
00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.176
Landscape, please, with the lake behind us.

55
00:02:28.456 --> 00:02:30.013
Okay... one, two, three!

56
00:02:30.293 --> 00:02:31.744
Let me take one more.

57
00:02:32.024 --> 00:02:33.432
Thank you so much!

58
00:02:33.712 --> 00:02:35.845
Would you like me to take one of you too?

59
00:02:37.195 --> 00:02:38.795
The conversation continues.

60
00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:40.334
Oh, yes please!

61
00:02:40.614 --> 00:02:41.787
That's kind of you.

62
00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:43.667
Where are you visiting from?

63
00:02:43.947 --> 00:02:45.078
From Germany.

64
00:02:45.358 --> 00:02:46.979
It's our first time in India.

65
00:02:47.259 --> 00:02:48.177
Welcome!

66
00:02:48.457 --> 00:02:50.633
Have you tried the local food yet?

67
00:02:50.913 --> 00:02:51.894
Not yet.

68
00:02:52.174 --> 00:02:53.497
Any suggestions?

69
00:02:54.847 --> 00:02:56.447
The conversation continues.

70
00:02:56.727 --> 00:02:59.777
Try the dal baati at the restaurant near the gate.

71
00:03:00.057 --> 00:03:01.380
It's famous here.

72
00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:03.690
Part 5.

73
00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.143
When things go wrong.

74
00:03:06.393 --> 00:03:07.609
We've lost our way.

75
00:03:07.889 --> 00:03:09.809
How do we get back to the main entrance?

76
00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.628
The guide is asking for more money than we agreed.

77
00:03:12.908 --> 00:03:14.657
Is this place safe after dark?

78
00:03:14.937 --> 00:03:17.497
Where's the nearest washroom or drinking water?

79
00:03:17.777 --> 00:03:20.337
I think I dropped my phone somewhere near the steps.

80
00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:22.260
Has anyone handed one in?

81
00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:24.549
Part 6.

82
00:03:24.829 --> 00:03:25.746
Practice.

83
00:03:26.996 --> 00:03:32.436
Turn these into polite questions: photo inside? close time? ticket price for children?

84
00:03:33.786 --> 00:03:34.703
Success:

85
00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:35.837
Answers.

86
00:03:36.117 --> 00:03:37.738
Can I take photos inside?

87
00:03:38.018 --> 00:03:39.319
What time does it close?

88
00:03:39.599 --> 00:03:41.519
How much is the ticket for children?

89
00:03:42.869 --> 00:03:43.808
Part 7.

90
00:03:44.088 --> 00:03:45.133
Speak today.

91
00:03:46.383 --> 00:03:49.818
Plan one weekend outing and say your itinerary in English.

92
00:03:50.098 --> 00:03:52.103
Learn 3 questions to ask a guide.

93
00:03:53.453 --> 00:03:54.989
That's the end of this lesson.

94
00:03:55.269 --> 00:03:59.941
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

95
00:04:00.221 --> 00:04:06.323
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

